1. Why is getline() preferred over cin >> productName for this exercise?
Because getline() detects spaces, while cin>> does not
2. Why is ceil() correct for box count even when the final box is not full?
Because it rounds it to the next highest integer, making sure that each product gets a box.
3. Which parts of this capstone demonstrate input, processing, output, type conversion, mathematical functions, and formatting?
std::getline() and std::cin are for input; subtotal, discountAmount, discountedTotal, and finalAmountDue are for processing,
std::cout is used for output, static_cast<double>() converts the integer into a double and ceil() back into an integer, 
td::ceil() rounds the exact fractional box requirement up to the next integer, 
and std::fixed paired with std::setprecision(2) enforces two decimal places for currency, while \t and \n align text and format line breaks.
